<title>JAPAN: Thai's Bangchak tenders to buy August crude.</title>
<headline>Thai's Bangchak tenders to buy August crude.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Bangchak Petroleum Plc said on Monday it had issued a tender to buy 800,000 barrels of Middle East crude oil and 300,000 barrels of Far East light sweet crudes for August loading.</p>
<p>The tender closes at 6 p.m. (1100 GMT) Bangkok time on Monday and is valid for 24 hours.</p>
<p>Sources said Bangchak is predominantly seeking Oman, Dubai, Murban or similar Gulf grades.</p>
